{
  "description": "How a screenplay is written, for the Mac and the desktop client: which element Tab and Return move on to, the line an element is set as, the edit Tab and Return make, and how a line sits on the page (its alignment, whether it is set in from both sides, bold or in the secondary ink) and which of its characters are markers that stay in the text but are not shown. The engine tells which element a line is; the client decides the rest. Locations and lengths are UTF-16 units, as the Mac counts them. Both clients pass every case.",
